          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:169d33371aa46ec73404c52601bb75e8322025ee5104cb34ebf7c0171d5e5e9b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c7d8a5f1540c4254a4e84c44b880d9bb",
      "statement": "A paused HITL run holds no token at all, only checkpointed graph state plus userId/threadId; because every resume is itself an authenticated BFF request, the BFF supplies a fresh subject token on every resume, which is why token lifetime is decoupled from pause duration.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/MCM-Architecture.md#L131-L140",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:10a8d69decb2fa50d8b2fe39cd9b6dd6fd10ea75ea8e0d84fe7ee02d88c0d615:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2dd1df7f2af643a7adba5fdd419cc1e3",
      "statement": "Per-user agent config (feature 018) is off by default, AES-256-GCM-encrypted at rest in the BFF-owned mcm-bff-db (physically separate from mc-db), decrypted only in-memory per run via resolveForRun(userId), and forwarded to the gateway via the X-Agent-Config header; the CopilotKit dock mounts only for a runnable config (enabled + provider credential + TMDB key).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/MCM-Architecture.md#L142-L152",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7b6e4c763866ea0dff96416f0faacbe0643abd990a334b032efc28dbce96a172:"
